[center][size=6][color=#00ccff][b]Absolute Suite @BUNDLE_VERSION@ Beta[/b][/color][/size]
[size=4][b][color=#ffaa00]One guided installer for Absolute Control, HOTAS flight, ship power, head tracking, and mouse steering.[/color][/b][/size]

[i]The ecosystem remains modular. Install only the gameplay modules you want, or use their standalone Nexus pages for independent updates.[/i][/center]

[line]

[center][size=5][color=#ffcc00][b]Included ecosystem[/b][/color][/size][/center]

[list]
[*][b][color=#00ff88]Absolute Control:[/color][/b] Required native suite menu, shared input capture, live presentation, and registry diagnostics.[/*]
[*][b][color=#00ff88]AbsoluteHOTAS:[/color][/b] Optional DirectInput HOTAS/HOSAS flight control, ship buttons, tuning, profiles, macros, and calibration.[/*]
[*][b][color=#00ff88]Absolute Power:[/color][/b] Optional priority-based ship-power presets and allocation controls.[/*]
[*][b][color=#00ff88]Absolute Head Tracking:[/color][/b] Optional OpenTrack-compatible rotational cockpit tracking.[/*]
[*][b][color=#00ff88]AbsoluteZero Mouse Steering:[/color][/b] Optional idle centering and locked-reticule mouse steering.[/*]
[/list]

[line]

[center][size=5][color=#00ccff][b]Standalone module pages[/b][/color][/size][/center]

[list]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/starfield/mods/17872][b]Absolute Head Tracking[/b][/url][/*]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/starfield/mods/17460][b]Absolute Zero[/b][/url][/*]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/starfield/mods/16668][b]Absolute HOTAS[/b][/url][/*]
[*][b]Absolute Power[/b] — standalone page coming soon[/*]
[/list]

Each standalone page remains the authoritative source for that module's full description, instructions, compatibility notes, changelog, and individual download.

[line]

[center][size=5][color=#00ccff][b]Install[/b][/color][/size][/center]

[list=1]
[*]Install the all-in-one archive with MO2 or Vortex.[/*]
[*]Use the guided installer to select the gameplay modules you want.[/*]
[*]Launch Starfield through SFSE.[/*]
[*]Open the Pause Menu and select [color=#ffaa00][b]MOD OPTIONS[/b][/color].[/*]
[*]Review each installed module, apply its settings, and test in a safe flight context.[/*]
[/list]

[b]Requirements[/b]
[list]
[*]Starfield 1.16.244.0[/*]
[*]SFSE 0.2.20 or later[/*]
[*]Address Library for SFSE Plugins for Absolute Control[/*]
[*]OpenTrack only for Absolute Head Tracking[/*]
[/list]

[line]

[center][size=5][color=#ffaa00][b]Safe modular ownership[/b][/color][/size][/center]

The bundle contains the same standalone DLLs and mod-owned default INIs supplied by the individual projects. It never includes or overwrites custom INIs, HOTAS profiles, logs, PDBs, or research builds.

[b]Selection warnings:[/b] Absolute Power ships preset shortcuts on number keys 1-4 until changed or cleared. AbsoluteZero is enabled by default and changes mouse-flight centering immediately. When AbsoluteZero and AbsoluteHOTAS are installed together, AbsoluteZero owns pitch and yaw, so a HOTAS stick cannot control those two axes; HOTAS continues to control roll, strafe, throttle, buttons, and profiles. Select that combination only when you want mouse pitch/yaw steering.

[line]

[center][size=5][color=#ffcc00][b]Beta boundaries and feedback[/b][/color][/size][/center]

This is a public ecosystem beta, not a promise that every hardware combination or mod stack has been covered. Power automation remains disabled by default. Head tracking is rotational only. Version-specific native operations fail closed when validation does not pass.

Please include the suite manifest, selected modules, Starfield/SFSE versions, hardware or tracker names, reproduction steps, and the relevant module log when reporting a problem.

